<section class="content" id="common-mistakes" aria-labelledby="mistakes-heading">
  <h2 id="mistakes-heading">Common Confusions and Pitfalls in GMT to NZST Calculations</h2>
  <article>
    <h3>Confusing NZST with NZDT</h3>
    <p>
      NZST is the standard winter time (UTC+12), while NZDT is the daylight saving time offset (UTC+13). Using the wrong offset when calculating time differences can result in a 1-hour scheduling error. Always verify the calendar date before applying the offset.
    </p>
  </article>
  <article>
    <h3>Assuming Auckland and Sydney share the same offset</h3>
    <p>
      Auckland (NZST, UTC+12) is 2 hours ahead of Sydney (AEST, UTC+10) during winter. If you apply Australian time offsets to New Zealand schedules, your meetings will be misaligned. Check local rules carefully.
    </p>
  </article>
</section>

